BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_317023564@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261121T065202Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T170000
SUMMARY:Lost Libraries of the Ancient World (LECTURES - 5TH ANNIVERSARY 2N
 D DATE)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n**The Toronto History Walks Explorer Pa
 ss is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\, em
 ail**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or for si
 gning up!**\n\n**A second date has been added as there are 9 on the waitli
 st for the Saturday October 24 lecture! If you are planning to take in thi
 s lecture\, get your spots early. See you then!**\n\nWe have an amazing "L
 ecture on the Go" series for 2026/2027. New topics and fascinating stories
  abound! Join me\, and uncover the world and keep active\, warm and cool d
 uring the winter and summer months!\n\nI started this walking classroom wh
 en we were under that horrible cloud called Covid. This series was popular
  and helped people get back into society and life. The first Lecture on th
 e Go was **Walking North America** and that was in October of 2021. Hard t
 o believe it's been 5 years of lectures. So I wanted to do something speci
 al to celebrate 5 years of exploration.\n\nThe "Lecture on the Go" Series 
 is open to members who have purchased the YEARLY MEMBERSHIP PASS\, it's fr
 ee for those members. If you wish to attend a lecture and you are not a ye
 arly pass member then the price **per** lecture is $20.00.\n\nLet's get st
 arted.\n\nWhat if some of humanity's greatest discoveries were made thousa
 nds of years ago\, and then lost forever?\n\nWhat if entire histories\, sc
 ientific breakthroughs\, literary masterpieces\, and eyewitness accounts o
 f the ancient world once existed\, only to disappear into the flames of wa
 r\, and the collapse of civilizations?\n\nJoin me for a fascinating journe
 y into the world's lost libraries\, from the legendary Library of Alexandr
 ia to the vanished collections of ancient empires whose treasures may be l
 ost forever.\n\nAt the heart\, stands the Library of Alexandria\, the most
  famous library in history. Founded over two thousand years ago\, it sough
 t to gather all the knowledge of the known world. Scholars from across the
  Mediterranean came to study astronomy\, mathematics\, geography\, medicin
 e\, philosophy\, and literature. Yet one of history's greatest mysteries r
 emains: what happened to this remarkable institution\, and what priceless 
 knowledge disappeared with it?\n\nWas it destroyed in a single catastrophe
 \, or did it slowly fade away over centuries from neglect?\n\nBeyond Alexa
 ndria\, we will explore a forgotten world of lost libraries and vanished c
 ollections stretching from Mesopotamia and ancient Egypt to medieval Europ
 e\, Baghdad\, and China. Discover the remarkable stories of librarians\, s
 cholars\, explorers\, and rulers who dedicated their lives to preserving k
 nowledge.\n\nWe will encounter lost books\, missing histories\, ancient sc
 ientific works\, and literary treasures that survive today only as fragmen
 ts.\nThis lecture is an exploration of one of history's most compelling qu
 estions: What have we forgotten?\n\nAnd how libraries shaped civilization 
 and why their loss continues to fascinate us centuries later. Whether you 
 are a lover of history\, literature\, archaeology\, or simply enjoy a good
  mystery\, this special Lecture on the Go will leave you wondering. What s
 ecrets of the past may still lie hidden\, just waiting to be rediscovered?
  Fascinating indeed!\n\nUpcoming topics in the 2026 series:\n\n\\*Philosop
 hy 1: Great Minds of the Western World: Goethe to Kant! - (2027)\n\\*Philo
 sophy 2: Great Minds of the Eastern\nWorld: Chuang Tzu to Dalai Lama - (20
 27)\nLegacy of Triangle: How a New York Factory Scandal changed North Amer
 ica - (September 2027)\n\nSo book your plans now!\n\nThis event is for all
  levels and walkers\, there are a few steps here and there to navigate\, b
 ut mostly on one level. This event in a non-walking event.\n\nThe lecture 
 begins on the steps of Old City Hall at the northeast corner of Bay Street
  and Queen Street West\, and\nhas a ticket price of $20.00 per person\, bu
 t **free with the yearly membership pass**.\n\n**Please note: Please e-tra
 nsfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-t
 ransfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/317023
 564/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261017T124036Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261017T124036Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_317361201@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261121T065202Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261129T111000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261129T141000
SUMMARY:Christmas on the Historic Toronto Islands! 
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t price when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the f
 ollowing email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nIt's hard to im
 agine a better place than the Toronto Islands\, as the big day approaches.
  Christmas on the islands was full of tradition\, of skating on the frozen
  Toronto Bay\, and sleigh rides between Ward's and Centre. And if it snows
  well so much the better. Let's take a look back at the Christmas season o
 n the Islands.\n\nIt's about growing up in Toronto. About the ten minute r
 ide over on the ferry boat\, and the memories that have made Toronto a sum
 mertime and wintertime city. It's a stretch of land that is historic and f
 ascinating\, both geologically and socially as well. And a history that br
 ings together the stories of Toronto from its founding.\n\nThe Gibraltar P
 oint Lighthouse was constructed in 1809\, and is one of the oldest structu
 res in Toronto.\n\nThe peninsula was partially severed by a storm in 1852\
 , which created a sandbar that was dangerously thin\, and the peninsula be
 came an island permanently by a violent storm that cut out the eastern cha
 nnel\, two hotels on the island were also destroyed. The modern history of
  the Islands' begins here!\n\nThe Islands' have three main parts\, and all
  three have their historic elements\, the most being the western most isla
 nd named for the Hanlan family. A spectacular hotel\, "The Ned Hanlan" was
  built and a regatta course dredged out of the western lagoon. An amusemen
 t park followed\, and an airport after that!\n\nIt was also a residential 
 enclave with most of the homes appearing on Ward's and Centre Islands. And
  the Christmas traditions began. A winter wonderland of lights and laughin
 g children and some adults as well. Shall we explore the islands?\n\nThe t
 our begins and ends at the Jack Layton Ferry Terminal at the foot of Bay S
 treet. We will meet **inside** the gates! And we will head over as a group
 \, so tickets must be bought before! Please meet 10 minutes before the mee
 tup time!\n\nThis tour has a ticket price of $15.00 per person!\n\n\\*\\* 
 **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket price when booking your space 
 for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontoh
 istorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/317361
 201/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261109T212507Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261109T212507Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_317516751@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261121T065202Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261204T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261204T140000
SUMMARY:City Place and Toronto's Historic Rail Lands! (NEW FOR 2026)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n**The Toronto History Walks Yearly Pass
  is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\, emai
 l**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or for sign
 ing up!**\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount whe
 n booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following em
 ail at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nBefore the soaring condomi
 nium towers\, landscaped parks\, trendy cafés and bustling streets of Cit
 yPlace\, you would have found yourself standing in the middle of one of To
 ronto's busiest railway landscapes!\n\nFor generations\, this was a world 
 of locomotives\, freight trains\, railway workers\, industrial buildings a
 nd miles of track stretching across the waterfront. These were the Railway
  Lands.\n\nAn enormous piece of Toronto's industrial heartland that helped
  keep the city moving and connected to the rest of Canada. But as the rail
 ways changed and their operations disappeared\, an opportunity emerged: wh
 at would Toronto do with all this land?\n\nThe story of CityPlace is a sto
 ry about ambition\, controversy\, urban planning and the ever-changing fac
 e of Toronto. From the grand redevelopment visions of the 1960s\, the arri
 val of the CN Tower and SkyDome\, to the plans that transformed these form
 er railway yards into one of Canada's most recognizable residential commun
 ities\, CityPlace has quite a story to tell.\n\nWe'll explore how an indus
 trial wasteland became a forest of condominium towers\, and how Toronto re
 connected with its waterfront\, and how an entirely new neighbourhood was 
 created virtually from scratch.\n\nLet's discover CityPlace\, a new neighb
 ourhood that many Torontonians know today in passing. A fascinating histor
 y overlooked. We'll look beyond the glass towers and modern architecture t
 o uncover the railway history\, the ambitious plans\, the personalities an
 d the decisions that shaped this corner of the city.\n\nToronto is constan
 tly reinventing itself\, but sometimes you have to look beneath the street
 s\, and even beneath the buildings\, to understand how it happened. Come a
 nd discover the remarkable transformation!\n\nThis walking tour begins at 
 Toronto Public Library - Fort York Branch\, at the corner of Bathurst Stre
 et and Fort York Blvd. The Bathurst Streetcar stops at the corner. We end 
 at The Well at the corner of Spadina and Front.\n\nThis walking tour is fo
 r all walking levels. Please dress for the season\, and hope to see you th
 ere.\n\nThis tour has a ticket price of $15.00 per person.\n\n\\*\\* **Ple
 ase note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for 
 this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohisto
 rywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/317516
 751/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261120T184152Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261120T184152Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_315328327@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261121T065202Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261205T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261205T140000
SUMMARY:THE LIFE AND TIMES OF JANE FRANKLIN  (LECTURES)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n**The Toronto History Walks Explorer Pa
 ss is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\, em
 ail**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or for si
 gning up!**\n\n**Toronto History Walks is currently working on bringing Le
 ctures on the Go to a permanent home for 2027. I will continue to update t
 his site for information as to the venue. But for now we will still meet o
 n the steps of Old City Hall until further notice.**\n\n**This is the last
  Lecture on the Go for 2026!**\n\nWe have an amazing "Lecture on the Go" s
 eries for 2027. New topics and fascinating stories abound! Join us and lea
 rn about the world and keep active and warm and cool during the winter and
  summer months!\n\nI started this walking classroom when we were under tha
 t horrible cloud called Covid. This series was popular and helped people g
 et back into society and life.\n\nThe "Lecture on the Go" Series is open t
 o members who have purchased the YEARLY MEMBERSHIP PASS\, it's free for th
 ose members. If you wish to attend a lecture and you are not a yearly pass
  member then the price **per** lecture is $20.00.\n\nJane Franklin was a p
 rominent 19th-century British woman known for her remarkable energy\, and 
 influence\, in exploration and colonial affairs during the Victorian era.\
 n\nShe is best remembered as the wife of John Franklin\, the Royal Navy of
 ficer who led the ill-fated Franklin Expedition. After her husband disappe
 ared in the Arctic in 1847\, Jane Franklin became one of the most determin
 ed figures in the search for him. She funded expeditions\, and lobbied the
  British government. She mobilized public attention for decades in an effo
 rt to uncover his fate and learn the truth.\n\nBut she wasn’t only defin
 ed by that search. Jane Franklin was also a widely travelled and intellect
 ually curious woman who visited places like Tasmania (then Van Diemen’s 
 Land)\, Greece\, the Middle East\, and Russia.\n\nShe also supported educa
 tion\, and science\, often working behind the scenes to influence institut
 ions like the Royal Geographical Society. You could say she became a kind 
 of unofficial power broker in British exploration.\n\nIn this lecture\, we
 ’ll explore the life and times of Jane Franklin. in the new biography se
 ries of timely women and men who made the world.\n\nUpcoming topics in the
  2027 series:\n\n\\*Philosophy 1: Great Minds of the Western World: Goethe
  to Kant! - (January 2027)\n\\*Philosophy 2: Great Minds of the Eastern\nW
 orld: Chuang Tzu to Dalai Lama - (January 2027)\nLegacy of Triangle: How a
  New York Factory Scandal changed North America - (February 2027)\nThe His
 tory of Masculinity from the Industrial Revolution to the 21st Century! (M
 arch 2027)\n\n**So book your plans now!**\n\nThis event is for all levels 
 and walkers\, there are a few steps here and there to navigate\, but mostl
 y on one level. This event in a non-walking event.\n\nThe lecture begins o
 n the steps of Old City Hall at the northeast corner of Bay Street and Que
 en Street West\, and\nhas a ticket price of $20.00 per person\, but **free
  with the yearly membership pass**.\n\n**Please note: Please e-transfer th
 e ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer 
 to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/315328
 327/
